        {
          "type": "text",
          "heading": "Scheduling",
          "text": "Events happen one at a time, at random times: each event of a flow moves one unit from its sources to its targets, with a probability per unit of the axis (its propensity) of the rate times its source for a proportional rate, or the rate for an absolute one. The engine stops at each impulse, where the impulses act first, and at each position where a rate jumps."
        },
